{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     comments — Ghost's comments, in an NSDS band.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ⚠ THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT USE NSDS'S .ns-comment MARKUP, and that is
     the whole decision worth recording here.

     NSDS draws a full comment thread — .ns-comment, __avatar, __head,
     __actions, __replies, .ns-commentform. Porting it would mean owning
     comment state: fetching threads, posting, editing, replying, moderating,
     rate-limiting, and member identity for every one of those. Ghost already
     ships all of it behind {{comments}}, rendered by its own bundle in an
     iframe.

     CLAUDE.md's rule decides it: check whether GHOST already supplies it
     before writing anything. It does. A hand-rolled thread would be the
     theme growing a third opinion — the exact failure abstract/09 records —
     and it would be the most expensive possible version, because it would be
     a third opinion about *user-generated content* rather than about styling.

     So the theme contributes the only two things Ghost cannot know: the band
     it sits in, and the fact that this site has a dark mode.

     ── color_scheme IS LOAD-BEARING ────────────────────────────────────────
     The comments bundle renders in an IFRAME, so the theme's stylesheet and
     [data-theme] cannot reach it. Left alone it renders light-on-white
     inside a dark page. "auto" makes it follow prefers-color-scheme, which
     is right for the two ends but NOT for a reader who has overridden the
     system with the theme toggle — theme-init.js writes that choice to
     [data-theme] on <html>, which the iframe cannot see.
     assets/js/1-theme/ owns re-syncing it; there is no server-side answer.

     GATING is Ghost's, not the theme's: @site.comments_enabled is 'all',
     'paid' or 'off', set in Admin → Settings → Comments. Rendering the band
     when it is 'off' would leave an empty heading on every post.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#unless (match @site.comments_enabled "off")}}
    <section class="ns-comments" id="comments">
        <div class="ns-comments__head">
            <h2 class="ns-comments__count">{{t "Responses"}}</h2>
        </div>
        {{comments color_scheme="auto"}}
    </section>
{{/unless}}
